{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices during downtrends (e.g., Feb 2024) by 5-10 EUR, failing to capture the speed of mean reversion.",
    "Adjust for upward bias in volatile regimes: During periods of high sentiment (e.g., May 2024 with values 1.00) and price spikes, the model underestimates the magnitude of rallies and subsequent volatility, predicting a flat trajectory instead of a surge.",
    "Reduce forecast horizon lag: The model exhibits a 'flat-line' behavior that lags behind actual price movements; apply a momentum multiplier to the first 5-10 days of the forecast when recent history shows a clear directional trend.",
    "Invert sentiment signal for short-term corrections: When sentiment history shows extreme values (1.00 or -1.00) immediately preceding the forecast, the model's static mean-reversion logic is insufficient; manually adjust the forecast to reflect the immediate directional pressure indicated by the sentiment spike.",
    "Apply mean-reversion dampening: After a sharp price spike (e.g., >70 EUR), the model fails to predict the subsequent drop; reduce the forecast by 2-3 EUR for the first 3 days following any price peak above the 30-day moving average."
  ]
}
